Well that ticks me off - I was just about to reply to a message when it
got expired out from under me!  ARGH!

Anyway - I had posted something a little while back about helms of opposite
alignment always being cursed, and then somebody posted a message saying,
"No they're not always cursed."

Well, I have to beg to differ.  All randomly generated helms of opposite
alignment are always cursed.  In other words, if you find a helm of OA on
a virgin level, it *WILL* be cursed.  (I checked the code.)

If you find one in a ghost pile, it almost certainly will be cursed - but
it's possible that the previous owner could have uncursed it.  The only
other spot where you might "find" an already uncursed helm of OA is if you
took a pile of uncursed armor and poly-piled it.  Poly-piling retains
blessings/cursings, so you would end up with an uncursed helm of OA.

Anyways...

